@startuml lease-recovery
title M-CB2: lease refusals and recovery - v0 slice 0 / Codex slice 1, design only

actor "Owner / operator\npinned OS principal; CLI under that UID" as Operator
participant "curator-run / later session runner\nagent UID + active generation\nexecutor and broker client" as Executor
participant "swarma-credential-broker\nunprivileged broker service UID" as Broker
database "Grant / revocation store\nbroker-owned durable state" as Grants
database "Helper ledger\nroot-owned; helper publishes generations" as Ledger
participant "Auth owner / provider adapter\ninside broker daemon, same UID\nCodex slice 1 only" as Adapter
participant "Existing service manager\nqualified writer containment / restore start check" as Manager
participant "Approved Codex executable\nbroker service UID; pinned digest" as Vendor
participant "Harness / private Codex app-server\nagent OS account" as Harness

note over Broker,Grants
  Broker also persists accounts/secrets, bindings, lease metadata
  and typed audit events; lease payload is never persisted (§8.3).
  Restore fence refuses bind, leases and renewals (§15.4);
  revocation.check is unavailable; prior verdict never waives final checks.
  Ledger is read directly, never inferred from an agent home (§4.2).
  [[../spec/broker.md#82-checks-in-order Spec §8.2]]
  [[../spec/broker.md#64-revocation Spec §6.4]]
end note

== Slice 0: admission before launch ==
Executor -> Executor : verify caller-composed plan and protected tuple
alt conflicting credential source or unqualified injection
  Executor -> Executor : credential_source_conflict / credential_injection_unavailable\nrefuse exec; no silent replacement (§12.2)
else executor checks pass
  Executor -> Broker : connect; kernel peer identity on both sides (§4.1)
  alt broker UID mismatch
    Executor -> Executor : server_identity_mismatch: send nothing
  else broker cannot obtain kernel peer UID
    Broker --> Executor : peer_identity_unavailable; refuse connection
  else peer identity available and server verified
    Executor -> Broker : lease.request (protected binding, network, launch_id)
    Broker -> Ledger : active UID + generation at bind / lease / renew
    Ledger --> Broker : record or read/parse/identity failure
    Broker -> Grants : verify lease chain AND caller chain\nagainst current revocations and R-TIME max/min windows under state lock
    Grants --> Broker : verified state or unavailable / revoked / invalid
    alt wrong role, inactive generation, chain, binding or account/profile/channel/network
      Broker --> Executor : role_not_permitted / principal_ledger_mismatch /\nlease_unbound / lease_not_authorised / lease_binding_mismatch / ...
      Executor -> Executor : do not exec; report typed refusal
      note over Executor,Broker
        Revoked lease/caller chain: lease_grant_revoked / lease_caller_revoked.
        Missing/malformed/unreadable revocations: revocation_state_unavailable.
        Unqualified harness: lease_harness_unqualified.
        Enforced network requirement in v0: lease_network_enforcement_unavailable.
        Recovery must satisfy current checks; no alternative login (§8.2, §12.2).
      end note
    else all checks 1-7 pass and restore fence open
      Broker --> Executor : lease/1 + payload
      Executor -> Executor : re-check tuple / sources immediately before exec
      alt tuple changed or source conflict
        Executor -> Executor : refuse exec (§12.2)\ncleanup after this refusal unspecified in spec §12.2
      else tuple still valid
        Executor -> Harness : exec with qualified env channel (§8.4)
        note over Executor,Harness
          Successful exec replaces executor; env harness is not a broker client.
          No return, post-exec release, renewal or report (§8.5).
          authorized_until bounds renewal; revocation stops new leases/renewals;
          unbind ends leases. Pre-exec release vs retain: unspecified in spec §18.7.
          stdin client lifetime / release point: unspecified in spec §18.7.
        end note
      end
    end
  end
end

== Durable revocation and crash boundary (v0) ==
Operator -> Broker : revocation.put (signed envelope)
alt malformed signature or unauthorised signer
  Broker --> Operator : typed refusal; revocation_not_authorised for signer authority (§6.4)
else valid authorised revocation
  Broker -> Grants : under state lock: temp write, flush, rename, directory flush
  alt crash after durable write, before acknowledgement
    note over Operator,Grants
      Durable revocation remains authoritative; not an empty set (§6.4).
      Startup/replay, lost-ack retry and partial-write recovery procedure:
      unspecified in spec §6.4; no retry protocol invented here.
    end note
  else publication continues
    Broker -> Broker : update memory
    Broker --> Operator : acknowledge only after durability
  end
end
Executor -> Broker : fresh launch client: next lease; or live holder: renewal\nafter service is available (not the exec-replaced env executor)
Broker -> Grants : read current revocation state
alt cannot read or parse
  Broker --> Executor : revocation_state_unavailable (all leases / renewals refused)
  Operator -> Grants : repair against current acknowledged history; restore follows §15.4
else affected lease or caller chain revoked
  Broker --> Executor : lease_grant_revoked / lease_caller_revoked
end
note over Executor,Harness : Copied tokens are not erased: expiry or vendor revocation only (§12.1).

== Independent fenced local restoration case (§15.4) ==
Operator -> Broker : close bind, leases and renewals; disable auto-start
Operator -> Operator : publish durable restore mark outside restored failure domain
Operator -> Manager : stop broker; contain / kill / confirm any vendor writers
Operator -> Grants : install protected snapshot while authorization remains closed
Manager -> Manager : every service-start path checks surviving restore mark/evidence
Broker -> Broker : fenced diagnostic operation only; revocation.check = unavailable
Operator -> Operator : reconcile complete acknowledged revocations against surviving\nexternal journal/checkpoint; resolve effects, time and companion restore obligations\nand writer/store evidence
alt complete acknowledged history survives
  Operator -> Grants : reconstruct and durably publish current revocations
else history missing / incomplete / unreadable
  Operator -> Operator : stay unavailable OR invalidate old roots and explicitly reissue rights
end
opt authority reconciled or explicitly replaced; reopen authorized
  Operator -> Operator : persist external reconciliation/reopen evidence, then clear mark
  Manager -> Manager : verify start check; recover service; publish readiness
  Broker -> Broker : only then open bind, leasing/renewal and current verdicts
  Operator -> Manager : re-enable auto-start last
end
note over Operator,Grants
  In-snapshot seq/audit/checkpoint cannot prove its own freshness.
  Interrupted restore/reopen remains closed. No stale snapshot repopulation.
  Revocation recovery does not resolve ambiguous vendor rotation.
  Concrete mark/start-evidence format unpublished (§18.8).
end note

== Disconnect is not release (v0, §8.5) ==
note over Executor,Broker
  Independent live-client scenario, not a continuation of the env exec.
  Close-on-exec disconnect leaves no executor to reconnect (§4.1, §8.5).
end note
Executor -> Executor : broker connection lost
Executor -> Broker : new connection; verify server UID; renew same lease_id
Broker -> Broker : require same (uid, generation, binding_id)\nactive lease before max(now, watermark) reaches authorized_until; repeat checks 1-7
alt ownership / lifetime / authorisation fails
  Broker --> Executor : lease_not_owner / lease_not_active / current check refusal
else checks pass
  note over Executor,Broker : Lease survives disconnect; no new principal or fallback source is authorised.
end

== Codex renewal (slice 1; adoption / release qualification pending, §18.4) ==
note over Executor,Harness
  Independent external-token scenario: live executor / later runner
  starts private app-server and remains client / lease holder (§9.3).
  It is not replaced by exec; env executor cannot run this renewal.
end note
Harness -> Executor : account/chatgptAuthTokens/refresh after 401
Executor -> Broker : lease.renew {lease_id, rejected_sha256} (default 8 s deadline)
Broker -> Broker : ownership + checks 1-7
alt current checks fail (including non-active account / unavailable owner)
  Broker --> Executor : typed refusal; no refresh material released
  Executor --> Harness : error answer; turn fails
  note over Broker,Adapter : Stopped owner sets owner_unavailable; recovery transition unspecified in spec §9.4.
else admitted and owner available
  Broker -> Adapter : bounded queue
  alt queue full or operation exceeds renewal deadline
    Broker --> Executor : renew_timeout
    Executor --> Harness : error answer; turn fails
  else queued within deadline
    Adapter -> Adapter : lock beside broker-owned home for read / refresh / reload
    break prior account writer / store / outcome unresolved
      Broker --> Executor : lease_owner_unavailable; no replacement refresh (§9.4)
      Executor --> Harness : error answer; turn fails
    end
    alt rejected token no longer current
      Adapter -> Adapter : use reloaded current token; no second refresh (§9.4)
    else rejected token still current
      Adapter -> Adapter : persist durable attempt intent before launch
      Adapter -> Manager : qualified contained launch of approved vendor executable
      Manager -> Vendor : at most one live account writer across replacement
      alt conclusively transient failure; writer/outcome resolved and retry safe
        Vendor --> Adapter : transient failure
        Adapter -> Adapter : account -> refresh_failed_transient\nbackoff only after writer/outcome resolution and while token valid
        note over Adapter,Broker
          Leases require active account (§8.2).
          Transient-to-active transition and exact failure-to-error mapping:
          unspecified in spec §9.4; no stale-token success invented.
        end note
      else timeout / daemon death / ambiguous rotation or unreadable evidence
        Manager -> Vendor : contain, kill and confirm writer absence before replacement
        Adapter -> Adapter : recover attempt; reload durable vendor home; no blind retry
        Adapter -> Adapter : owner_unavailable or reauth_required if outcome unresolved
        Broker --> Executor : refuse renewal; no fallback material
        Executor --> Harness : error answer; turn fails
      else refresh token rejected
        Vendor --> Adapter : rejection
        Adapter -> Adapter : account -> reauth_required
        Broker --> Executor : lease_reauth_required
        Executor --> Harness : error answer; turn fails
        Operator -> Broker : re-enrol after writer absence through fresh vendor ceremony (§9.2, §9.4)
      else refreshed
        Vendor --> Adapter : refreshed broker-owned login
        Adapter -> Adapter : confirm writer lifecycle; reload durable home; persist outcome
      end
    end
    opt current token available and account active
      Adapter --> Broker : reloaded access token + account ID
      Broker -> Broker : repeat authorisation, R-TIME and restore fence under state lock immediately before release
      alt still authorised and within deadline
        Broker --> Executor : renewed access token + account ID
        alt account ID matches lease
          Executor --> Harness : correlated refresh answer
          Harness -> Harness : retry call
        else account ID differs
          Executor -> Executor : verification fails; do not send token\nerror/recovery unspecified in spec §9.3
        end
      else operation misses deadline
        Broker --> Executor : renew_timeout
        Executor --> Harness : error answer; turn fails
      else authorisation revoked / expired
        Broker --> Executor : current authorisation refusal; no material
        Executor --> Harness : error answer; turn fails
      end
    end
  end
end
opt live external-token holder releases when ending execution (§8.5)
  Executor -> Broker : lease.release {lease_id} (idempotent; ends renewal)
end
note over Executor,Broker
  Exact teardown/release ordering and init-failure / runner-loss cleanup:
  unspecified in spec §18.7. Without release, authorized_until bounds
  renewal; revocation stops new leases/renewals; unbind ends leases.
  Automatic lease-state transitions / cleanup scheduling are unpublished (§8.5).
end note
note over Executor,Harness
  Refusal/timeout: no late or uncorrelated answer, no fallback login (§9.3-§9.4).
  No launch auth.json; ephemeral storage; private app-server per execution.
  Refresh token stays in broker store. Claude has no auth owner:
  a surviving client's credential_error report affects only lease;
  env-exec reporter is unspecified in spec §18.7; owner marks account;
  recovery is re-enrol + restart, --resume transcript (§10.1, §8.5).
  [[../spec/broker.md#85-renewal-release-and-reports Spec §8.5]]
  [[../spec/broker.md#93-external-token-mode Spec §9.3]]
  [[../spec/broker.md#94-refresh-and-states Spec §9.4]]
end note
note over Broker,Grants
  R-TIME: durable watermark, trusted advances only; expiry at max,
  not_before at min; untrusted time refuses new leases/renewals (§15.1).
  Expiry binding removal also needs boot-inclusive monotonic lifetime;
  missing elapsed evidence delays removal, never permits credentials.
  Reset/restore cannot revive genuinely expired authority.
  R-GEN companion restore: user manager ledger and dispatcher effects
  reconcile independently; stale active ledger is not freshness (§15.4).
end note
note over Broker,Vendor
  R-SVC-EGRESS v1: vendor network only through dedicated proxy;
  no direct fallback; login/refresh/policy-fetch and resolver rows qualified.
  Safe proxy failure is transient only after writer/outcome resolution.
  R-FATE fate table is owned by user manager §7 (§9.4, §15.2).
  R-LOCK: no state lock across synchronous platform calls;
  per-record marker and late-result fences preserve final checks (§13.1).
end note
note over Executor,Broker
  R-REBIND removes old binding and ends its leases, retains tombstone,
  then admits fresh binding for same UID/generation with current authority.
  Old lease cannot renew under new binding. Fresh-lease handoff OPEN;
  explicit park/restart keeps account until handoff is qualified (§18.11).
end note
@enduml
